---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PillBadge from '../components/PillBadge.astro';
---

<Layout title="seed-db — Documentation" description="Comprehensive documentation for seed-db: setup, commands, flags, config, waterfall heuristics, DAG resolution, safety, and error contract." currentPath="/docs">
  <div class="surface-aluminium min-h-screen py-10 border-b border-[#c7ccd2]">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
        <!-- STICKY SIDEBAR NAVIGATION -->
        <aside class="hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3">
          <div class="sticky top-24 surface-panel p-4 space-y-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] uppercase tracking-wider px-2">
              ON THIS PAGE
            </div>
            <nav class="space-y-1 font-mono text-xs">
              <a href="#quick-start" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Quick start
              </a>
              <a href="#commands" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Commands
              </a>
              <a href="#flags" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Flags
              </a>
              <a href="#config-file" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Config file
              </a>
              <a href="#how-values-are-chosen" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                How values are chosen
              </a>
              <a href="#insert-order" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Insert order
              </a>
              <a href="#without-a-live-database" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Without a live database
              </a>
              <a href="#safety" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Safety
              </a>
              <a href="#errors-and-exit-codes" class="docs-nav-link block px-3 py-2 rounded text-[#4a4f56] hover:text-[#0a0a0a] transition-all">
                Errors and exit codes
              </a>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- MAIN DOCUMENTATION CONTENT -->
        <article class="lg:col-span-9 space-y-16">
          <!-- Title & Pre-release Callout -->
          <div class="space-y-4 pb-6 border-b border-[#9aa1a8]">
            <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] tracking-tight">
              Documentation
            </h1>
            <p class="font-sans text-base text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
              Everything you need to seed a PostgreSQL database with seed-db, in the order you will need it.
            </p>
            <div class="surface-panel p-4 text-xs font-sans text-[#0a0a0a] leading-relaxed">
              <strong class="font-mono">Notice:</strong> seed-db is pre-release. Version 0.0.1 only reserves the package name, so these docs describe version 1 as designed. The commands below are the plan, not something you can install today.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- 1. QUICK START -->
          <section id="quick-start" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Quick start</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                seed-db works with PostgreSQL, one schema per run (default <span class="code-chip">public</span>). Three commands take you from nothing to seeded data.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <!-- Step 1 -->
              <div class="surface-panel p-5 space-y-3 card-lift">
                <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span>1.</span> Set up
                </h3>
                <div class="rounded-lg bg-[#0c0d10] p-3 border border-[#2c3036] flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-white">
                  <span class="font-bold"><span class="text-[#8a9199] select-none">$ </span>seed-db init</span>
                  <button class="doc-copy-btn h-[32px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors" data-copy="seed-db init">Copy</button>
                </div>
                <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                  Asks for your database URL and a default row count. Writes <span class="code-chip">seed.config.ts</span> and <span class="code-chip">.env.example</span>. It refuses to overwrite existing files unless you pass <span class="code-chip">--force</span>.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Step 2 -->
              <div class="surface-panel p-5 space-y-3 card-lift">
                <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span>2.</span> Look
                </h3>
                <div class="rounded-lg bg-[#0c0d10] p-3 border border-[#2c3036] flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-white">
                  <span class="font-bold"><span class="text-[#8a9199] select-none">$ </span>seed-db inspect</span>
                  <button class="doc-copy-btn h-[32px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors" data-copy="seed-db inspect">Copy</button>
                </div>
                <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                  Prints your tables, columns, relationships, the insert order, and which generator each column will use. Nothing is written. Add <span class="code-chip">--json</span> to print the schema as JSON.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Step 3 -->
              <div class="surface-panel p-5 space-y-3 card-lift">
                <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span>3.</span> Seed
                </h3>
                <div class="rounded-lg bg-[#0c0d10] p-3 border border-[#2c3036] flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-white">
                  <span class="font-bold"><span class="text-[#8a9199] select-none">$ </span>seed-db run</span>
                  <button class="doc-copy-btn h-[32px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors" data-copy="seed-db run">Copy</button>
                </div>
                <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                  Generates data and inserts it in one transaction. If anything fails, everything rolls back. Add <span class="code-chip">--dry-run</span> to print the SQL, or <span class="code-chip">--check</span> to run it all and roll back.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 2. COMMANDS -->
          <section id="commands" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Commands</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                Three commands. One sets up, one shows you what it understands, one does the work.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
              <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Command</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">What it does</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a]">
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">seed-db init</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Interactive setup. Writes seed.config.ts and .env.example. Refuses to overwrite unless --force.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">seed-db inspect</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Reads the database and prints tables, columns, relationships, insert order, and the generator chosen for each column. --json prints the schema model.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">seed-db run</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Generates data and inserts it. --dry-run prints the SQL. --check runs everything and rolls back.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 3. FLAGS -->
          <section id="flags" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Flags</h2>
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#4a4f56]">seed-db run</h3>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
              <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Flag</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">What it does</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a]">
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">-t, --tables &lt;a,b&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Seed only these tables. Default: all tables in the schema. Missing parent rows are sampled from rows that already exist.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">-r, --rows &lt;n&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Rows per table. Default 10, or defaultRows from your config.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--seed &lt;n&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Seed the random generator. Same seed, same data.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--dry-run</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Print the SQL and change nothing.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--check</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Run the full seed inside the transaction, report the result, then roll back. Exit code 0 means a real run would succeed.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--out &lt;file&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Write the INSERT statements to a file instead of a database. The tool assigns the keys.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--start-id &lt;n&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">First integer key in file mode. Default 1.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--snapshot &lt;file&gt;</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Read the schema from an inspect --json snapshot. inspect accepts it too.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--yes</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Skip the confirmation prompt for non-local hosts.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-2 pt-4">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#4a4f56]">Flags for every command</h3>
              <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
                <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Flag</th>
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">What it does</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">-c, --config &lt;path&gt;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Config file. Default ./seed.config.ts.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--database-url &lt;url&gt;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Database to connect to.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--schema &lt;name&gt;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Schema to use. Default public.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--format &lt;text|json&gt;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Output format. --json is shorthand for --format json.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold whitespace-nowrap">--verbose</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Show extra detail, including the raw database error.</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel p-4 text-xs font-sans text-[#4a4f56] space-y-2">
              <p>
                <strong class="text-[#0a0a0a] font-mono">Precedence order:</strong> Command-line flags first, then <span class="code-chip">seed.config.ts</span>, then the <span class="code-chip">DATABASE_URL</span> environment variable, then built-in defaults.
              </p>
              <p class="text-[#6b727a]">
                After version 1: <span class="font-mono">--schema-file</span> (read a pg_dump file). Version 1 reads a live database or a snapshot.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 4. CONFIG FILE -->
          <section id="config-file" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Config file</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                You only need a config file when the tool guesses a column wrong. Everything else works without it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
              <span class="code-chip">seed.config.ts</span> is optional. Use it to set fixed values, write your own generators, or skip tables.
            </p>

            <!-- Code Snippet in Silver Frame -->
            <div class="silver-frame">
              <div class="bg-[#0c0d10] border border-[#2c3036] rounded-[18px] p-5 relative group">
                <div class="text-xs font-mono text-[#8a9199] mb-2">seed.config.ts</div>
                <pre class="font-mono text-xs text-[#f4f6f8] leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">import type &#123; SeedConfig &#125; from "seed-db"; // type-only, so it loads in the compiled binary

export default &#123;
  databaseUrl: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
  defaultRows: 50,
  seed: 42,
  tables: &#123;
    users: &#123;
      rows: 200,
      columns: &#123;
        status: (&#123; faker &#125;) =&gt; faker.helpers.arrayElement(["active", "suspended"]),
        tenant_id: "fixed-tenant-uuid-1234",
        age: &#123; int: &#123; min: 18, max: 90 &#125; &#125;,
      &#125;,
    &#125;,
    _prisma_migrations: &#123; ignore: true &#125;,
  &#125;,
&#125; satisfies SeedConfig;</pre>
                <button
                  class="doc-copy-btn absolute top-4 right-4 h-[36px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors"
                  data-copy='import type { SeedConfig } from "seed-db";

export default {
  databaseUrl: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
  defaultRows: 50,
  seed: 42,
  tables: {
    users: {
      rows: 200,
      columns: {
        status: ({ faker }) => faker.helpers.arrayElement(["active", "suspended"]),
        tenant_id: "fixed-tenant-uuid-1234",
        age: { int: { min: 18, max: 90 } },
      },
    },
    _prisma_migrations: { ignore: true },
  },
} satisfies SeedConfig;'
                >
                  Copy
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Top-level Options Table -->
            <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Top-level options</h3>
              <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
                <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Option</th>
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Default</th>
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Meaning</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a] font-sans">
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">databaseUrl</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">DATABASE_URL</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Database to connect to.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">schema</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">public</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Schema to seed.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">defaultRows</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">10</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Rows per table.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">seed</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">none</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Random seed. Same as --seed.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">nullRate</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">0.1</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Chance (0 to 1) that a nullable column is NULL.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">allowedHosts</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">none</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Hosts that skip the confirmation prompt.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">tables</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-[#6b727a]">none</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Per-table settings: ignore, rows, columns.</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Column Rules Table -->
            <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Column rules</h3>
              <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
                <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Rule</th>
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Example</th>
                      <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Result</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a] font-sans">
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A constant</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">"fixed-tenant-uuid-1234"</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Every row gets that value.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Pick from a list</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">&#123; oneOf: ["a", "b"], weights: [3, 1] &#125;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Random pick, optionally weighted.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A whole number</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">&#123; int: &#123; min: 18, max: 90 &#125; &#125;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Random integer in the range.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A decimal</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">&#123; float: &#123; min: 0, max: 1, precision: 2 &#125; &#125;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Random decimal in the range.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A faker path</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">&#123; faker: "internet.email" &#125;</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Uses that faker generator.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Your own function</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">(&#123; faker, index, row &#125;) =&gt; ...</td>
                      <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Return any value. Use the supplied faker, not Math.random(), or --seed stops being repeatable.</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel p-4 text-xs font-sans text-[#4a4f56]">
              The config is checked when it loads. An unknown table, an unknown column, or a rule that cannot fit the column exits with code 2 and names the key.
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 5. HOW VALUES ARE CHOSEN -->
          <section id="how-values-are-chosen" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">How each column gets its value</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                For every column it tries five things in order and uses the first one that applies.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
              <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold w-16">Order</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Rule</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Example</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a] font-sans">
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">1</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Skip it. The database fills it in.</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Auto IDs, defaults, computed columns.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">2</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Your rule. Anything in seed.config.ts wins.</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">status: &#123; oneOf: [...] &#125;</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">3</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Foreign key. Pick a real ID from the parent table.</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]"><span class="code-chip">orders.user_id</span> gets an existing <span class="code-chip">users.id</span></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">4</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Name match. The column name says what it holds.</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]"><span class="code-chip">email</span> gets an email, <span class="code-chip">phone</span> gets a phone number</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono font-bold">5</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Type fallback. Use the column type.</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Text gets words, numbers get numbers, dates get dates</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
              Nullable columns are NULL about 10% of the time. Change that with <span class="code-chip">nullRate</span>. Run <span class="code-chip">seed-db inspect</span> to see which rule each column will use before anything is written.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 6. INSERT ORDER AND CIRCULAR TABLES -->
          <section id="insert-order" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Insert order and circular tables</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                Parent tables are filled before the tables that point at them.
              </p>
            </div>

            <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
              seed-db draws an arrow from every table to the tables it needs, then fills tables whose parents are done. Ties break alphabetically, so the order never changes.
            </p>

            <!-- Inspect Terminal Box -->
            <div class="silver-frame">
              <div class="bg-[#0c0d10] border border-[#2c3036] rounded-[18px] p-5 font-mono text-xs space-y-2 text-[#c7ccd2]">
                <div class="text-[#8a9199]"><span class="text-white select-none">$</span> seed-db inspect</div>
                <div class="space-y-1 pt-2">
                  <div class="flex justify-between text-white"><span class="font-bold">1</span> employees <span class="text-[#8a9199]">10 rows</span> <span class="text-[#c7ccd2]">manager_id deferred (self-reference)</span></div>
                  <div class="flex justify-between text-white"><span class="font-bold">2</span> products <span class="text-[#8a9199]">10 rows</span></div>
                  <div class="flex justify-between text-white"><span class="font-bold">3</span> users <span class="text-[#8a9199]">10 rows</span> <span class="text-[#8a9199]">user_id &lt;- users.id</span></div>
                  <div class="flex justify-between text-white"><span class="font-bold">4</span> orders <span class="text-[#8a9199]">10 rows</span> <span class="text-[#8a9199]">order_id &lt;- orders.id, product_id &lt;- products.id</span></div>
                  <div class="flex justify-between text-white"><span class="font-bold">5</span> order_items <span class="text-[#8a9199]">10 rows</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-3 border-t border-[#2c3036] text-white font-bold">
                  Patch pass: employees.manager_id
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Circular Situations Table -->
            <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
              <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Situation</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">What happens</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a] font-sans">
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A table points at itself, and the link can be empty</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">The link is inserted empty, then filled by one update after all inserts.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Two tables point at each other, and one link can be empty</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">That link only is deferred. Both tables are inserted, then the link is patched.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">A circle where every link is required (NOT NULL)</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#0a0a0a] font-bold">No valid first row exists. seed-db stops with exit code 3, prints the circle, and tells you to make one link nullable or deferrable.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 7. WITHOUT A LIVE DATABASE -->
          <section id="without-a-live-database" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Without a live database</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                You can use seed-db without ever giving it your real database.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Subsection 1 -->
            <div class="surface-panel p-5 space-y-4">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Snapshot, then a SQL file</h3>
              <div class="rounded-lg bg-[#0c0d10] p-4 border border-[#2c3036] font-mono text-xs text-white space-y-1 relative group">
                <div>seed-db inspect --json &gt; schema.json</div>
                <div>seed-db run --snapshot schema.json --out seed.sql --seed 1</div>
                <div>psql mydb -f seed.sql</div>
                <button
                  class="doc-copy-btn absolute top-3 right-3 h-[32px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors"
                  data-copy="seed-db inspect --json > schema.json && seed-db run --snapshot schema.json --out seed.sql --seed 1 && psql mydb -f seed.sql"
                >
                  Copy
                </button>
              </div>
              <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                A snapshot holds table and column names and types only. It has no rows and no connection details, so it is safe to share. The SQL file is plain INSERT statements. You can read it before you run it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Subsection 2 -->
            <div class="surface-panel p-5 space-y-4">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Run it, then roll it back</h3>
              <div class="rounded-lg bg-[#0c0d10] p-3 border border-[#2c3036] font-mono text-xs text-white flex items-center justify-between">
                <span class="font-bold">seed-db run --check --seed 1</span>
                <button class="doc-copy-btn h-[32px] px-3 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white bg-[#1b1d22] hover:bg-[#2a2d33] border border-[#454a52] transition-colors" data-copy="seed-db run --check --seed 1">Copy</button>
              </div>
              <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#4a4f56] leading-relaxed">
                Check mode runs every insert and ends with a rollback. It proves a real run would succeed and leaves nothing behind. Sequences still advance.
              </p>
              <p class="font-sans text-xs text-[#6b727a]">
                SQL file mode assumes the target tables are empty. The tool assigns primary keys itself, starting at 1. Change the start with <span class="code-chip">--start-id</span> if your tables already hold rows.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 8. SAFETY -->
          <section id="safety" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <PillBadge text="IN PLAIN WORDS" isDark={false} />
              <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-[#0a0a0a]">Safety</h2>
              <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#4a4f56]">
                It asks before touching anything that is not on your own machine.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="surface-panel overflow-hidden">
              <table class="w-full text-left font-sans text-xs border-collapse">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="border-b border-[#9aa1a8] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ffffff] to-[#cfd4da] font-mono text-[#0a0a0a]">
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Protection</th>
                    <th class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">How it works</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#b9c0c8] text-[#0a0a0a] font-sans">
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] whitespace-nowrap">One transaction</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Every real run is a single transaction. Any error rolls everything back.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] whitespace-nowrap">Confirmation for other hosts</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">If the database host is not localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1, and not listed in allowedHosts, run prints the target and asks to continue. Pass --yes to skip. --dry-run never asks.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] whitespace-nowrap">No surprises in CI</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">Nothing prompts when output is not a terminal.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="hover:bg-[#ffffff]/50 transition-colors">
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-[#0a0a0a] whitespace-nowrap">No telemetry</td>
                    <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-[#4a4f56]">It connects only to the database you give it.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 9. ERRORS AND EXIT CODES -->
          <section id="errors-and-exit-codes" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-24">
